# Generated files. The Gemini review leaves their content out of the diff it reads and lists them
# instead (xtask/src/review.rs); GitHub collapses them in diffs. The review reads this file as it
# was at the merge base, so a pull request cannot hide its own code by marking it generated, and
# this file is a gate file.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated
**/.sqlx/** linguist-generated
web/src/generated/** linguist-generated
web/pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated

# Diff drivers. The review's diff shows each Rust change with its whole function (git diff
# --function-context), which needs a language's function boundaries; git's rust driver knows
# Rust's, nested items included. git has no driver for TypeScript, YAML or TOML, so their changes
# keep three lines of context (FUNCTION_DRIVERS in xtask/src/git.rs).
*.rs diff=rust
